{% for passage in passages %}
[{{ passage.n }}]{% if passage.speaker %} {{ passage.speaker }}:{% endif %} {{ passage.text }}
{% endfor %}

Cite passages by number. Do not copy quote text. When a fact uses information from another passage, such as the date
a defined term like "the Effective Date" stands for, cite that passage too.
For each fact, list the things it mentions by name, with a short lowercase kind for each (such as "company",
"person", "agreement", "court", or "product") and a role: "subject" for what the fact is mainly about, otherwise
"about". Use each thing's full name, and list other names the document uses for it as aliases, such as a defined
short name ("Vega" for Vega Components Corp.) or an abbreviation. When the text gives an exact date the fact takes effect, write it as valid_from. When it gives an exact date
the fact ends or is due, write it as valid_until. When the text gives a start date and a length of time, such as
"for six months from April 1, 1999", compute the end date. Resolve relative dates against the document's date. Use
ISO-8601 with a timezone, such as 2027-01-01T00:00:00Z. Leave either out when no exact date follows from the text.

Answer with JSON only:
{"facts": [{"text": "...", "passages": [1], "mentions": [{"name": "...", "kind": "...", "role": "subject", "aliases": []}],
"valid_from": null, "valid_until": null}]}
